<title>UK: Wachovia Bank sets $250 million 12-year bond.</title>
<headline>Wachovia Bank sets $250 million 12-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Lehman Brothers.</p>
<p> BORROWER   WACHOVIA BANK OF NORTH CAROLINA</p>
<p> AMT    $250 MLN	COUPON     **	  MATURITY    17.OCT.08</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    17.OCT.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  40 BP     REOFFER    **	  SPREAD	+43 BP</p>
<p> NOTES	**TO BE PRICED</p>
<p> MOODY	AA2	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA+	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    NEW YORK  HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    15 BP     SELL CONC  25 BP     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND W/I 10-YEAR U.S. TREASURY -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
